\section{Elements in every object}{
\itemize{
\item \code{specification}: the frozen model. Rows, landscape bins, formulas,
priors, and the reference standardization are fixed here once and reused
by every method. See "Read the specification".
\item \code{parameters}: a named list of seven numeric vectors that defines the
parameter layout and holds starting values. It contains no estimates.
See "Find each parameter".
\item \code{call}: the matched call to \code{\link[=multiScale_bayes]{multiScale_bayes()}}.
\item \code{inference}: a label for the computation, one of \code{"prepared"},
\code{"full Bayesian NUTS"}, \code{"full Bayesian slice sampling"},
\code{"joint Laplace Gaussian approximation"},
\code{"marginal Laplace with scale-SD quadrature"}, or
\code{"importance-corrected marginal Laplace"}.
\item \code{inference_metadata}: a description of what the object estimates. See
"Read the inference metadata". Fits saved by older versions of the
package can lack it, and they remain usable.
}
